                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- To see cells, we need a tool that can magnify the image of the leaf.\n- Binoculars are used to see distant objects, so they are not suitable for this task.\n- Reading glasses are used to help people with presbyopia see things up close, but they do not magnify the image.\n- A magnifying glass can magnify the image, but it may not provide enough magnification to see cells clearly.\n- A microscope is designed specifically for viewing small objects like cells, and it can provide high magnification and resolution.\n\nTherefore, the best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf is a microscope.\n\nAnswer: B) microscope",
