                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Piano playing is a skill that requires practice and training. It is not something that is inherited genetically.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a physical change?\n2. What is an inherited trait?\n3. What is a life function?\n4. What is a learned behavior?\n5. Is playing piano a physical change?\n6. Is playing piano an inherited trait?\n7. Is playing piano a life function?\n8. Is playing piano a learned behavior?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A physical change is a change in the physical properties of a substance, such as its shape, size, or state of matter.\n2. An inherited trait is a characteristic that is passed down from parents to offspring through genes.\n3. A life function is a process that is necessary for an organism to stay alive, such as respiration, digestion, or reproduction.\n4. A learned behavior is a behavior that is acquired through experience or training.\n5. Playing piano is not a physical change because it does not involve a change in the physical properties of the piano or the player.\n6. Playing piano is not an inherited trait because it is not determined by genes.\n7. Playing piano is not a life function because it is not necessary for the player to stay alive.\n8. Playing piano is a learned behavior because it requires practice and training to develop the skill.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4fa5a06b-fefc-40a4-96d3-c5ddb6a0fbf6",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) a learned behavior.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
