                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) A physical characteristic refers to a feature or trait of an organism's body or appearance. This does not apply to the bird's experience of eating the insect.\n\nB) A learned behavior is a behavior that an organism acquires through experience or observation. In this case, the bird learns to avoid eating brightly-colored insects after experiencing the bad taste.\n\nC) An inherited behavior is a behavior that is passed down from one generation to another through genes. This does not apply to the bird's experience of eating the insect, as it is not a behavior passed down genetically.\n\nD) An adaptation is a characteristic or behavior that helps an organism survive and reproduce in its environment. While the bird's avoidance of brightly-colored insects may help it survive, this is not an adaptation in itself.\n\nBased on these definitions, the best answer is B) a learned behavior.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4a329fc3-b893-4056-99c0-c2fa8fc4c424",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) a learned behavior.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
