                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Animals have different ways of adapting to their environment, including physical characteristics, inherited behaviors, and learned behaviors.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a learned behavior?\n2. How do animals learn to avoid certain foods?\n3. Is the bird's avoidance of the brightly-colored insect a physical characteristic or a learned behavior?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A learned behavior is a behavior that an animal develops through experience or observation.\n2. Animals can learn to avoid certain foods through trial and error, or by observing other animals that have had negative experiences with the food.\n3. The bird's avoidance of the brightly-colored insect is a learned behavior, as it learned to avoid the insect after experiencing its bad taste. Therefore, the best answer is B) a learned behavior.",
                        "answers": [
