                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the meaning of the term \"learned\" in the context of animal characteristics.\n2. Research the characteristics of wolves.\n3. Analyze each characteristic to determine if it is innate or learned.\n4. Identify the characteristic that is most likely learned.\n\nAnswer: \nThe characteristic of wolves that is most likely learned is D) social behavior. While fur color, eyesight, and litter size are innate characteristics that are determined by genetics, social behavior is largely influenced by environmental factors and learned behaviors. Wolves learn how to interact with other members of their pack, establish dominance, and communicate through vocalizations and body language. Therefore, social behavior is the most likely characteristic of wolves that is learned.",
