                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Wolves are social animals that live in packs and have complex social behaviors.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are some examples of social behaviors exhibited by wolves?\n2. Are these social behaviors innate or learned?\n3. If they are learned, what is the most likely characteristic that is learned?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Examples of social behaviors exhibited by wolves include hunting together, communicating through vocalizations and body language, and caring for their young.\n2. These social behaviors are learned through observation and interaction with other wolves in the pack.\n3. The most likely characteristic that is learned is social behavior, as it is essential for wolves to live and function in a pack.",
