                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " We know that a learned behavior is something that an animal does after being taught by another animal or by observing its environment. A good way to eliminate some of the choices is to think about which of these things could be taught. For example, we know that you can't teach an animal to have hollow, light-weight bones. This is something that animals are born with. We also know that you can't teach an animal to have white feathers on the throat. This is something that animals are born with. This leaves us with two choices, laying eggs to reproduce and avoiding insects that taste bad. We know that animals can be taught to avoid insects that taste bad. For example, a mother bird might teach her chicks to avoid insects that taste bad. Therefore, the answer is D.",
