                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain which of the following involves a learned behavior?\n\nProfessor: Sure, I can help you with that. Which options are you considering?\n\nStudent: I'm considering all of them.\n\nProfessor: Okay, let's go through each one. Laying eggs to reproduce is a natural behavior that is instinctual, so it's not a learned behavior. Having hollow, light-weight bones is a physical characteristic that is determined by genetics, so it's not a learned behavior either. Avoiding insects that taste bad is a learned behavior because it involves the animal learning through experience which insects are safe to eat and which ones are not. Finally, having white feathers on the throat is also a physical characteristic that is determined by genetics, so it's not a learned behavior.\n\nStudent: I see. So, the answer is C) avoiding insects that taste bad.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Do you have any other questions about this topic?",
