                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The two black guinea pigs are both heterozygous (Bb) for fur color. This means that they each carry one dominant black allele (B) and one recessive white allele (b). \n\nTo determine the possible fur colors of their offspring, we can use a Punnett square. \n\n|   | B | b |\n|---|---|---|\n| B | BB | Bb |\n| b | Bb | bb |\n\nEach box in the Punnett square represents a possible combination of alleles that could be passed down from the parents to their offspring. The uppercase letters represent the dominant black allele (B) and the lowercase letters represent the recessive white allele (b). \n\nFrom the Punnett square, we can see that there are two possible genotypes for the offspring: BB (homozygous dominant black) and Bb (heterozygous black). \n\nSince black fur is dominant, both BB and Bb genotypes will result in black fur. Therefore, the answer is A) 100% black.",
