                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: If two guinea pigs with black fur (Bb) are bred, what will be the color of their offspring?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Black fur is dominant over white fur in guinea pigs.\n- The two black guinea pigs are both heterozygous (Bb) because they have one dominant black allele (B) and one recessive white allele (b).\n- When two heterozygous guinea pigs are crossed, their offspring can inherit either the dominant black allele (B) or the recessive white allele (b) from each parent.\n- Therefore, the possible genotypes of the offspring are BB, Bb, or bb.\n- BB and Bb genotypes will result in black fur, while bb genotype will result in white fur.\n- The probability of each genotype can be determined using a Punnett square: \n\n|   | B | b |\n|---|---|---|\n| B | BB | Bb |\n| b | Bb | bb |\n\n- The Punnett square shows that there is a 25% chance of the offspring having the BB genotype (black fur), a 50% chance of having the Bb genotype (black fur), and a 25% chance of having the bb genotype (white fur).\n- Therefore, the answer is D) 75% black, 25% white.\n\nAnswer: D) 75% black, 25% white.",
