                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what you mean by dominant and recessive traits?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Dominant traits are those that are expressed even if only one copy of the gene is present, while recessive traits are only expressed if two copies of the gene are present.\n\nStudent: So, in this case, black fur is dominant and white fur is recessive?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct.\n\nStudent: Okay, so if two black guinea pigs (Bb) are crossed, what are the possible genotypes of their offspring?\n\nProfessor: The possible genotypes of their offspring are BB, Bb, and bb.\n\nStudent: And what do those genotypes mean in terms of fur color?\n\nProfessor: BB and Bb both result in black fur, while bb results in white fur.\n\nStudent: So, what are the ratios of the possible fur colors in their offspring?\n\nProfessor: The ratio would be 3:1, with 75% black (BB and Bb) and 25% white (bb).\n\nStudent: Got it. So the answer is D) 75% black, 25% white.\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a730ca15-5f7b-4056-9e7c-1810dcc8c94d",
