                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Write out the genotypes of the parent guinea pigs.\n\nBoth parent guinea pigs are Bb, meaning they each have one dominant black allele (B) and one recessive white allele (b).\n\nStep 2: Use a Punnett square to determine the possible genotypes of the offspring.\n\n|   | B | b |\n|---|---|---|\n| B | BB| Bb|\n| b | Bb| bb|\n\nEach parent can pass on either a B or a b allele to their offspring. The Punnett square shows that there are four possible combinations of alleles in the offspring: BB, Bb, Bb, and bb.\n\nStep 3: Determine the phenotype (physical appearance) of each genotype.\n\nBB and Bb both have the dominant black allele, so they will have black fur. Only bb has the recessive white allele, so it will have white fur.\n\nStep 4: Calculate the ratio of black to white offspring.\n\nThere are two possible genotypes that result in black fur (BB and Bb) and one possible genotype that results in white fur (bb). Therefore, the ratio of black to white offspring is 3:1.\n\nStep 5: Choose the answer that matches the ratio of black to white offspring.\n\nD) 75% black, 25% white is the answer that matches the ratio of black to white offspring calculated in step 4.",
                        "answers": [
