                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Recall the definition of each term.\n- Atom: the basic unit of a chemical element, consisting of a nucleus of protons and neutrons, with electrons in orbit around the nucleus.\n- Reactant: a substance that takes part in and undergoes change in a chemical reaction.\n- Element: a substance consisting of atoms that all have the same number of protons; cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means.\n- Compound: a substance composed of two or more elements chemically combined in definite proportions.\n\nStep 2: Identify the substances involved in the reaction: hydrogen and oxygen.\n\nStep 3: Recall that when hydrogen and oxygen combine, they form water.\n\nStep 4: Determine which term best describes water in this reaction based on the definitions:\n- Water is not an atom because it is composed of multiple atoms (two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom).\n- Water is not a reactant because it is the product of the reaction, not a substance that undergoes change.\n- Water is not an element because it is composed of multiple elements (hydrogen and oxygen).\n- Therefore, the correct answer is D) a compound.\n\nStep 5: Double-check the answer to ensure it makes sense and is supported by the information given. In this case, it does: water is indeed a compound composed of hydrogen and oxygen atoms chemically combined in a fixed ratio.",
