                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: \n- Static electricity is the buildup of electric charges on an object.\n- Like charges (positive-positive or negative-negative) repel each other, while opposite charges (positive-negative or negative-positive) attract each other.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the charge of the balloons?\n2. What happens when two objects with the same charge are brought close to each other?\n3. What happens when two objects with opposite charges are brought close to each other?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The question states that the balloons are positively charged.\n2. Like charges repel each other, so the balloons will not come together. This eliminates option C.\n3. Opposite charges attract each other, so the balloons will not move apart. This eliminates option A.\n4. Since the balloons are both positively charged, they cannot transfer electrons to each other to balance out their charges. Therefore, neither balloon will gain or lose a charge. This eliminates options B and D.\n \nTherefore, the answer is none of the above.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
