                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain the question again?\n\nProfessor: Sure, Ariana is using balloons to investigate static electricity. The question is asking what will happen when she brings two positively charged balloons close to each other.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what does it mean for the balloons to be positively charged?\n\nProfessor: It means that they have an excess of positive charges, or protons.\n\nStudent: Got it. So, what are the answer choices again?\n\nProfessor: The answer choices are A) The balloons will move apart. B) One balloon will lose its charge. C) The balloons will come together. D) One balloon will gain a negative charge.\n\nStudent: Hmm, I think it might be C or D. Can you explain why?\n\nProfessor: Sure. When two objects with the same charge are brought close together, they will repel each other, so A is not the answer. B is also not correct because it doesn't explain what will happen to the other balloon. So, that leaves us with C and D. If the balloons come together, it means that they have opposite charges and are attracted to each other, so C is not correct. That leaves us with D, which is the correct answer. One balloon will gain a negative charge to balance out the positive charge of the other balloon, and they will be attracted to each other.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e9d0a956-996c-40fa-ab9f-7d096406ac9d",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) One balloon will gain a negative charge.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
