                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) mass number.\n\nExplanation:\n- Valence refers to the number of electrons in the outermost shell of an atom, which determines its chemical reactivity.\n- Chemical property refers to the behavior of an atom in chemical reactions, which is determined by its electron configuration and valence.\n- Electrical charge refers to the net charge of an atom or ion, which is determined by the number of protons and electrons.\n- The sum of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom is called the mass number, which is a fundamental property of the atom that determines its isotopic identity and nuclear stability.",
