                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: \n- Protons have a positive charge and are located in the nucleus of an atom.\n- Neutrons have no charge and are also located in the nucleus of an atom.\n- The number of protons in an atom determines its atomic number and its identity as an element.\n- The sum of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom determines its mass.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of valence?\n2. What is the definition of chemical property?\n3. What is the definition of electrical charge?\n4. What is the relationship between protons, neutrons, and the mass of an atom?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Valence refers to the number of electrons in the outermost shell of an atom, which determines its reactivity and ability to form chemical bonds.\n2. Chemical property refers to the behavior of a substance in a chemical reaction, such as its ability to react with other substances or undergo a change in composition.\n3. Electrical charge refers to the property of matter that causes it to experience a force when placed in an electric field, either positive or negative.\n4. The sum of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom determines its mass, which is measured in atomic mass units (amu). The number of protons in an atom determines its atomic number and its identity as an element, while the number of neutrons can vary within the same element and result in different isotopes with different masses. The mass number is the sum of the number of protons and neutrons in an atom. Therefore, the answer to the original question is B) mass number.",
                        "answers": [
