                        "cot": "A) Mass number: Protons and electrons have different masses, with protons being much heavier than electrons. So, they are not equal in mass number.\n\nB) Kinetic energy: The kinetic energy of protons and electrons depends on their velocities, which can vary in different situations. So, they are not always equal in kinetic energy.\n\nC) Sign of charge: Protons have a positive charge, while electrons have a negative charge. So, they have opposite signs of charge.\n\nD) Magnitude of charge: Protons and electrons both have a charge of 1 elementary charge unit, but with opposite signs. So, they are equal in the magnitude of charge.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) magnitude of charge.",
