                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) sign of charge.\n\nProtons and electrons are subatomic particles that have opposite charges. Protons have a positive charge, while electrons have a negative charge. Therefore, in terms of their charge, they are always equal in sign. This means that if a proton has a charge of +1, an electron will always have a charge of -1. So, the correct answer is C) sign of charge. \n\nOption A) mass number is incorrect because protons and electrons have vastly different masses. Protons have a mass of approximately 1 atomic mass unit (amu), while electrons have a mass of approximately 0.0005 amu.\n\nOption B) kinetic energy is incorrect because the kinetic energy of a particle depends on its mass and velocity. Since protons and electrons have different masses, they will have different kinetic energies at the same velocity.\n\nOption D) magnitude of charge is incorrect because protons and electrons have opposite charges of equal magnitude. The charge of a proton is +1, while the charge of an electron is -1. Therefore, the magnitude of their charges is the same, but the sign is different.",
                        "answers": [
