                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "How are protons and electrons always equal?\nA) Do they have the same mass number?\nB) Do they have the same kinetic energy?\nC) Do they have the same sign of charge?\nD) Do they have the same magnitude of charge?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Protons and electrons are both subatomic particles found in atoms.\n- They have different properties, such as mass and charge.\n- The mass number of an atom is the sum of its protons and neutrons, so protons and electrons do not have the same mass number.\n- Kinetic energy depends on the velocity of the particle, so protons and electrons do not necessarily have the same kinetic energy.\n- Protons have a positive charge, while electrons have a negative charge, so they do not have the same sign of charge.\n- However, protons and electrons have the same magnitude of charge, which is 1.602 x 10^-19 Coulombs.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) magnitude of charge.",
