                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Protons and electrons are subatomic particles that make up atoms. Protons have a positive charge and are located in the nucleus of an atom, while electrons have a negative charge and orbit around the nucleus.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the charge of a proton?\n2. What is the charge of an electron?\n3. How do the charges of protons and electrons compare to each other?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The charge of a proton is positive.\n2. The charge of an electron is negative.\n3. Protons and electrons have opposite charges, meaning that they are not equal in terms of charge sign.\n\nConclusion:\nIn what respect are protons and electrons always equal? The answer is none of the above options (A, B, or D). The only respect in which protons and electrons are always equal is their charge magnitude, which is equal in magnitude but opposite in sign. Therefore, the correct answer is C) sign of charge.",
