                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Recall the definitions of exothermic and endothermic reactions.\n\n- Exothermic reaction: A chemical reaction that releases heat to the surroundings.\n- Endothermic reaction: A chemical reaction that absorbs heat from the surroundings.\n\nStep 2: Consider the statement \"When cold temperatures are produced in a chemical reaction.\"\n\n- This statement suggests that heat is being removed from the surroundings, which means the reaction is absorbing heat.\n- Therefore, the reaction is endothermic.\n\nStep 3: Check the answer choices.\n\n- A) Exothermic: This is the opposite of what we determined in Step 2, so it is not the correct answer.\n- B) Endothermic: This matches our conclusion in Step 2, so it is the correct answer.\n- C) Suspension: This term refers to a mixture in which small particles are dispersed in a liquid or gas but do not settle out. It is not related to the temperature change in a chemical reaction.\n- D) Vaporization: This term refers to the conversion of a liquid or solid into a gas. It is not related to the temperature change in a chemical reaction.\n\nStep 4: Select the answer.\n\n- The correct answer is B) endothermic.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3b114d02-2fce-4b32-a600-c59fef45e32d",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
