                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what is meant by cold temperatures in a chemical reaction?\n\nProfessor: Sure, cold temperatures refer to a decrease in temperature during a chemical reaction.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what is an exothermic reaction?\n\nProfessor: An exothermic reaction is a chemical reaction that releases heat into the surroundings, resulting in an increase in temperature.\n\nStudent: And what about an endothermic reaction?\n\nProfessor: An endothermic reaction is a chemical reaction that absorbs heat from the surroundings, resulting in a decrease in temperature.\n\nStudent: So, if a chemical reaction produces cold temperatures, it must be an endothermic reaction?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. When a chemical reaction results in a decrease in temperature, it is an endothermic reaction.\n\nStudent: And what about suspension and vaporization? Are they related to cold temperatures in a chemical reaction?\n\nProfessor: No, suspension and vaporization are not related to cold temperatures in a chemical reaction. Suspension refers to a mixture of solid particles in a liquid, while vaporization refers to the conversion of a liquid or solid into a gas.",
