                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to understand that decreasing the heat energy of a gas means lowering its temperature. With that in mind, the answer is A) condensation. When the temperature of a gas is lowered, its particles lose energy and move slower, which can cause them to come closer together and form a liquid. This process is called condensation. Evaporation (B) and vaporization (D) are the opposite of condensation and require an increase in heat energy to occur. Radiation (C) is the transfer of heat energy through electromagnetic waves and is not directly related to the temperature of a gas.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
