                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Condensation: This is the process where a gas turns into a liquid when it loses heat energy. Since we are decreasing the heat energy of a gas, condensation is a possible result.\n\nB) Evaporation: This is the process where a liquid turns into a gas when it gains heat energy. Since we are decreasing the heat energy, evaporation is not a possible result.\n\nC) Radiation: This refers to the emission of energy as electromagnetic waves. While radiation can be related to heat transfer, it is not a direct result of decreasing the heat energy of a gas.\n\nD) Vaporization: This is the process where a liquid turns into a gas when it gains heat energy. Similar to evaporation, since we are decreasing the heat energy, vaporization is not a possible result.\n\nSo, the correct answer is A) condensation.",
                        "answers": [
