                    {
                        "id": "612a53c2-714c-40d7-a5a4-131416f3225a",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify what happens to gas when heat energy is decreased.\n2. Match the result with the given options.\n3. Choose the correct option.\n\nAnswer:\n1. When heat energy is decreased, the gas molecules lose energy and move slower, causing the gas to cool down and potentially change state.\n2. A) Condensation occurs when a gas is cooled and changes into a liquid. B) Evaporation occurs when a liquid is heated and changes into a gas. C) Radiation is the transfer of heat energy through electromagnetic waves. D) Vaporization occurs when a liquid is heated and changes into a gas.\n3. The correct option is A) condensation, as decreasing the heat energy of a gas can cause it to cool and change into a liquid.",
                        "answers": [
