                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the most suitable tool for observing a soil sample?\nTo answer this question, we need to consider the properties of the tools listed and their potential usefulness in observing a soil sample. \n\nA) Camera - While a camera can capture images of a soil sample, it may not provide the level of detail needed for observation and analysis. \n\nB) Compass - A compass is not useful for observing a soil sample as it is designed to determine direction. \n\nC) Hand lens - A hand lens is a magnifying glass that can be used to observe small details of a soil sample, making it the most suitable tool for this purpose. \n\nD) Telescope - A telescope is designed for observing distant objects and is not suitable for observing a soil sample. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) hand lens.",
