                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What tools should a baker use to measure the volume and temperature of water needed to prepare dough for baking bread?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The baker needs to mix 2 cups of flour with 1 cup of water.\n- The water needs to be at a specific temperature of 85\u00b0F.\n- To measure the volume of water, the baker needs a tool that can accurately measure cups.\n- To measure the temperature of water, the baker needs a tool that can accurately measure degrees Fahrenheit.\n- Option A (a balance and a ruler) does not include a tool for measuring temperature.\n- Option B (a balance and a thermometer) includes a tool for measuring temperature, but a balance is not necessary for measuring volume.\n- Option C (a measuring cup and a balance) includes a tool for measuring volume, but a balance is not necessary for measuring volume.\n- Option D (a measuring cup and a thermometer) includes both a tool for measuring volume and a tool for measuring temperature.\n\nTherefore, the best tools for the baker to measure both the volume and temperature of the water are a measuring cup and a thermometer. The answer is D.",
