                        "cot": "C) solution.\n\nExplanation:\nWhen a substance (sugar in this case) is dissolved in a liquid (water in this case), it forms a homogeneous mixture called a solution. The substance that is being dissolved is called the solute, and the liquid in which it is dissolved is called the solvent. In this scenario, sugar is the solute and water is the solvent, and together they form a solution. A suspension, on the other hand, is a heterogeneous mixture in which the particles of the solute are large enough to settle out over time. Since the sugar dissolves completely in the water, it is not a suspension. Therefore, the correct answer is C) solution.",
