                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is created when a student dissolves a spoonful of sugar in a glass of water?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- When a substance dissolves in another substance, it creates a mixture.\n- The substance that gets dissolved is called the solute.\n- The substance that does the dissolving is called the solvent.\n- The resulting mixture is called a solution.\n- In this scenario, the sugar is the solute and the water is the solvent.\n- Therefore, the answer is C) solution.\n\nAnswer: C) solution.",
