                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's consider the states of matter for each substance:\n- Ice is solid water, which means its molecules are tightly packed and have low energy. This indicates that it has a low temperature.\n- Water is liquid, which means its molecules have more energy and are moving more freely than in ice. This indicates that it has a higher temperature than ice.\n- Steam is gaseous water, which means its molecules have even more energy and are moving rapidly. This indicates that it has the highest temperature of the three.\n\nSo, the order from coldest to hottest is ice, water, steam. The correct answer is A) ice, water, steam.",
