                    {
                        "id": "d089f441-37b8-4c88-9672-d3b533803728",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Determine the temperature at which water freezes and boils.\n2. Compare the temperatures of ice, water, and steam to the freezing and boiling points of water.\n3. Order the substances from coldest to hottest based on their temperature in relation to the freezing and boiling points of water.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Water freezes at 0\u00b0C (32\u00b0F) and boils at 100\u00b0C (212\u00b0F).\n2. Ice is below 0\u00b0C, so it is colder than the freezing point of water. Steam is above 100\u00b0C, so it is hotter than the boiling point of water. Water is between 0\u00b0C and 100\u00b0C.\n3. Based on the above information, the order from coldest to hottest is A) ice, water, steam.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "856220f7-c90f-4064-99e5-67c7b12664f8",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
