                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: In what order are water, ice, and steam arranged from coldest to hottest?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Water, ice, and steam are all forms of H2O.\n- At standard pressure, water freezes at 0\u00b0C and boils at 100\u00b0C.\n- Ice is frozen water, so it has a temperature below 0\u00b0C.\n- Steam is water vapor, so it has a temperature above 100\u00b0C.\n- Therefore, the order from coldest to hottest is: ice, water, steam.\n\nAnswer: A) ice, water, steam.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "eebd8aae-fe93-4d32-90ed-35dd5cbe7a7d",
