                    {
                        "id": "4167c654-0d55-4c2b-9118-753087cb2902",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Water, ice, and steam are all different states of the same substance, H2O. The temperature at which water freezes is 0\u00b0C, and the temperature at which water boils is 100\u00b0C at standard atmospheric pressure.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. At what temperature does ice exist?\n2. At what temperature does water exist?\n3. At what temperature does steam exist?\n4. What is the order of temperatures for ice, water, and steam?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Ice exists at temperatures below 0\u00b0C.\n2. Water exists at temperatures between 0\u00b0C and 100\u00b0C.\n3. Steam exists at temperatures above 100\u00b0C.\n4. The order from coldest to hottest is A) ice, water, steam.",
