                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Recall the properties of solids.\n2. Identify the options that describe the motion of molecules in solids.\n3. Eliminate the options that do not fit the properties of solids.\n4. Choose the option that best describes the motion of molecules in a solid object.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Solids have a fixed shape and volume.\n2. Options A and C describe the molecules vibrating in place, which is a property of solids.\n3. Option B describes the motion of molecules in a gas, which is not a property of solids. Option D describes the motion of molecules in a liquid, which also is not a property of solids.\n4. Therefore, the best statement that describes the motion of molecules of a solid object is A) They vibrate in place within a fixed volume.",
