                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Solids are one of the three states of matter, along with liquids and gases. In a solid, the molecules are tightly packed together and have a fixed shape and volume.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of a solid?\nAnswer: A solid is a state of matter in which the molecules are tightly packed together and have a fixed shape and volume.\n\n2. How do the molecules of a solid object move?\nAnswer: The molecules of a solid object vibrate in place.\n\n3. Does the shape of a container affect the motion of the molecules in a solid object?\nAnswer: No, the shape of a container does not affect the motion of the molecules in a solid object.\n\nAnswer to the original question: A) They vibrate in place within a fixed volume.",
