                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is A) navigate ships.\n\nExplanation:\n\nCenturies ago, before the invention of modern navigation tools, people relied on their knowledge of the stars to navigate ships across the seas. By observing the position of the stars in the sky, sailors could determine their location and plot a course to their destination. This technique, known as celestial navigation, was essential for long-distance travel and exploration. Therefore, option A) navigate ships is the correct answer. \n\nOption B) study the weather is incorrect because although people did observe the stars to predict weather patterns, it was not their primary use of star knowledge. \n\nOption C) predict volcanic eruptions is also incorrect because there is no evidence to suggest that people used their knowledge of the stars to predict volcanic eruptions. \n\nOption D) map the Earth's surface is also incorrect because while people did use the stars to create maps, it was not their primary use of star knowledge.",
