                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that while satellite technology can help predict the weather, it cannot prevent storms from occurring. With that in mind, the most likely benefit of developing this technology is that it will help warn people about dangerous storms. This can allow people to take necessary precautions and evacuate if necessary, potentially saving lives and minimizing damage. It may also help with disaster preparedness and response efforts. While it may indirectly show people that science is interesting, and could potentially help with driving in the rain by providing more accurate weather forecasts, these are not the primary benefits of this technology.",
