                    {
                        "id": "c2a24783-5284-4c4f-9319-01540f0284d5",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Satellites are used to gather data about weather patterns and can provide information about temperature, precipitation, wind speed, and cloud cover. This data can be used to create weather forecasts and predict severe weather events.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of developing new satellite technology for weather prediction?\n2. How does satellite technology gather data about weather patterns?\n3. What can be done with the data gathered by satellite technology?\n4. How can weather forecasts and predictions benefit people?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The purpose of developing new satellite technology for weather prediction is to improve the accuracy and timeliness of weather forecasts and predictions, which can help people prepare for and respond to severe weather events.\n2. Satellite technology gathers data about weather patterns by using sensors to measure temperature, precipitation, wind speed, and cloud cover. This data is transmitted back to Earth for analysis.\n3. The data gathered by satellite technology can be used to create weather forecasts and predictions, which can help people plan their activities and make informed decisions about travel, outdoor events, and emergency preparedness. The data can also be used by meteorologists and emergency responders to track severe weather events and issue warnings to the public.\n4. Weather forecasts and predictions can benefit people by helping them avoid dangerous weather conditions, plan their activities, and make informed decisions about travel and emergency preparedness. Accurate and timely weather information can also help reduce the risk of property damage, injury, and loss of life during severe weather events. Therefore, the most likely benefit of developing new satellite technology for weather prediction is that it will help warn people about dangerous storms (option C).",
                        "answers": [
