                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain how developing new satellite technology to predict the weather will benefit people?\n\nProfessor: Sure, developing this technology will most likely benefit people by helping to warn them about dangerous storms.\n\nStudent: How will it do that?\n\nProfessor: Well, the new satellite technology will be able to gather more accurate and detailed information about weather patterns, which will allow meteorologists to make more precise predictions about when and where severe weather events like hurricanes, tornadoes, and thunderstorms will occur.\n\nStudent: So, if people know when and where these storms will happen, they can take steps to protect themselves?\n\nProfessor: Exactly. They can evacuate areas that are at risk of flooding or wind damage, or take shelter in safe locations. This can help save lives and prevent property damage.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. Will this technology also help people drive in the rain?\n\nProfessor: While the technology may provide more accurate information about when and where rain will occur, it is not specifically designed to help people drive in the rain. However, it may indirectly benefit drivers by providing more accurate weather forecasts, which can help them plan their travel routes and avoid areas that are likely to be affected by severe weather.",
